#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105745 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105602 :question/id #uuid "7bfabbd2-9988-5c0e-9c17-3d430b3e7a0f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4699" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n![](images/97/9773630254747a4bbd072bd44a6263bdd078fa09005b1bb5f51c48b894d67daf.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n![](images/43/43b9b089e0f93e63acf386bb605a0e3751cc8660899ce19d23835f9f79918bcc.svg)\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y = 0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx - 3y = 1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n![](images/4a/4a598a80f2f14715d1f10d182b3f80887c7586beabecc2a329119b624c19a4fa.svg)\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨1+3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "97cd9132-458b-5234-a3d2-22b633acb74c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049422 :topic/math-academy-id 151 :topic/title "Solving 2x2 Systems of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/math-academy-id 493 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551473 :question-generator/id #uuid "e0f0d1a1-c3b4-5f13-83aa-ac207126bbb9" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186105745.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00f46691-e757-5abf-9bd0-72673d154024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326944} {:answer/id #uuid "1f03cf88-a33c-5f4d-ad02-3f006b794c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327202} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab00714-7708-5dae-8ab3-51d79a90b326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327854} {:answer/id #uuid "83e07d41-124b-5fc8-8112-a63a06c47867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328074} {:answer/id #uuid "e8ac4687-189d-52a1-91e7-5e515f849261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8ac4687-189d-52a1-91e7-5e515f849261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328970} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b2a178f-52c0-5a56-a7a5-d0eb67f8a442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329348}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6118a9d-772a-5b19-befb-3156e01fd7c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42155" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=3 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3+y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9f1382a-870c-5f7c-b007-6684dc65136e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1 - 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104027} {:answer/id #uuid "e68d6a57-2fff-5fe1-97e2-53e0d4e0fb15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1 + 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104028} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0db42e-1100-5418-8315-c630442bb8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104029} {:answer/id #uuid "56c35cf2-8374-5cfd-8ca3-d7861125849e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 1 + 2y, y⟩, y ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104030} {:answer/id #uuid "7ec12860-5f4a-5e06-8d80-fe18641609f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104031}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a117e6ad-ea85-5ffa-be6d-c20de27fa2cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7b917a4-149a-5335-87b0-b5af432e1dd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379836} {:answer/id #uuid "d5fcad4a-a362-5ebf-bbea-e056e83246a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379837} {:answer/id #uuid "63ca10a3-6abf-594c-bc38-1b37ffcbdc38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379838} {:answer/id #uuid "1730136e-f78b-5eda-af0d-81956b5fce34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379839} {:answer/id #uuid "72d559c6-a1d1-5e3e-be26-d5a5b1c9e977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1730136e-f78b-5eda-af0d-81956b5fce34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379839} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b446b32-d3dd-5edb-b643-a1c5a81e8d04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379835}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0407db63-d38b-50cb-b37f-dfd7ce1a8b10" :question/math-academy-id "q-42156" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=1+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨1+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17febf8e-1aa5-5cbf-bf1d-e9987976f9a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263229} {:answer/id #uuid "3cdfe373-1c05-5f22-9ed5-ccf0f4dd9b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263544} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6d9d6a-1705-5b61-8129-44a0f7d4d0f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264328} {:answer/id #uuid "ad82aa2b-ee84-5336-bc4d-46cbfde0facc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}y-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264491} {:answer/id #uuid "df7ef948-6ddd-520b-b34c-48ba7514f083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-y-3 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b6d9d6a-1705-5b61-8129-44a0f7d4d0f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264328} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a1e99c9-d9c5-5879-a3eb-f47e2e0715ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265263}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "527da09a-4044-5c93-b906-dff9203cb12d" :question/math-academy-id "q-130922" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 6 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+3y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3y-1,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3y-1 \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3y-1 \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c247114-0265-5d19-950c-d6ddadbc52e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284888} {:answer/id #uuid "290d4310-b38e-58a7-b7f8-229614a89956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285148} {:answer/id #uuid "2bad0c5b-8898-5e4a-8e57-39537797a08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285168} {:answer/id #uuid "606e281f-cd18-58f3-89f3-488a6defa97e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285672} {:answer/id #uuid "e873edde-7317-52df-9cf0-cc4cec745284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286914}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bad0c5b-8898-5e4a-8e57-39537797a08c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285168} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9e4910b-9053-5d68-9d88-04077e065b78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287630}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "64e30738-40d0-5a54-8cdd-1cc83ec4b628" :question/math-academy-id "q-20782" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 14 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -7 & 14 & 21\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-2y=-3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-3+2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3+2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15f1cb44-5b06-5d4d-9607-9ad3cbf2af14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284985} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6fcd9a-23a6-5453-9d08-4d210d1b7d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285795} {:answer/id #uuid "7c25a4a3-f7cb-549a-ae3e-01af8eacb8bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285932} {:answer/id #uuid "9d5c5078-f3f5-5c82-bd8d-335557d74371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286228} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9ee132-1b40-541a-bae6-15241f57f92e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7-3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d6fcd9a-23a6-5453-9d08-4d210d1b7d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285795} :answer-field/id #uuid "53d20d8e-decf-56db-bd2e-b51650f71249" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287334}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25615c72-6956-5e2b-84cd-a6850d4c806d" :question/math-academy-id "q-20958" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 28\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 28\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=7 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=7.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=7+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=7+3y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7+3y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e575bf2-282a-56e0-9c7b-f9d668c70fd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340104} {:answer/id #uuid "81c756d9-3c31-59cb-a4e0-7950314357f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340296} {:answer/id #uuid "a1613f2b-9f40-56d7-b338-827222fcc89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340591} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5a603a-0d9e-53c5-965d-695328e8649e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340920} {:answer/id #uuid "ce31b1b2-1883-577c-b531-35a7f77096b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca5a603a-0d9e-53c5-965d-695328e8649e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340920} :answer-field/id #uuid "d185127d-bb7a-5f18-8d05-fdf27c7419f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341748}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99972d7b-41c2-573c-8100-907314a5a411" :question/math-academy-id "q-73524" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 12 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -16 & 8 \\\\ 