+(-8){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1-2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392488 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bce7c5fc-118d-57ed-b7b7-198ec9740ae2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392490} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d36658-bde5-5a80-bfa7-5f01e189d3c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392491} {:answer/id #uuid "882a5fb0-4677-57cd-a0eb-b59850dc71e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6-4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392492} {:answer/id #uuid "8f92d555-2375-53e0-8687-b595e26d132d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392493} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8fa779-e3c8-583f-924d-8c09429656f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392494}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f92d555-2375-53e0-8687-b595e26d132d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392493} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ddc2483-85ad-5618-94ab-3e0c00d11533" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392489}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d49a7f92-7486-5a6e-9890-b6f6940d9011" :question/math-academy-id "q-42160" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 8 & -12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y &=6 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-4y=6.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=6+4y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=6+4y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6+4y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402782 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6429a97e-1ea2-5116-bdb0-c323c42ac6b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402784} {:answer/id #uuid "7529729a-7538-57b4-bb95-683aba7b3a43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402785} {:answer/id #uuid "0937d732-3e23-55bb-bb34-82a9a014fa2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3+2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402786} {:answer/id #uuid "3e199bd5-5ebe-5592-b9f0-829bfdc64fe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402787} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8c9956-92cc-5dc7-bdf2-6e23c0868904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-3y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402788}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6429a97e-1ea2-5116-bdb0-c323c42ac6b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402784} :answer-field/id #uuid "e33c2e04-873c-5d06-b295-2871dc81bbfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402783}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41fb9598-c5d7-5a4e-b94b-50dacda69952" :question/math-academy-id "q-42158" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "The system corresponding to $M$ is \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=3 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=⟨3-2y,\\,y⟩,\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403689 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22cd6aa9-a925-5038-975c-07e44d80e350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403691} {:answer/id #uuid "0e0364cb-677b-524e-aa38-691178112aba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2+y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403692} {:answer/id #uuid "6274e549-fa07-5abb-bd6c-53630d47a7b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403693} {:answer/id #uuid "11509ba5-2bfa-5670-b24e-690396084002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2-y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403694} {:answer/id #uuid "da9d2dd8-4de7-59f6-8ae5-f0b3a20d355b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22cd6aa9-a925-5038-975c-07e44d80e350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403691} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ccee7c5-bc00-583c-adcd-616a8af7768b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403690}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28d32302-16b0-5cdc-a69e-754fd94318a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-73740" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+2y=-1.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=-1-2y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-1-2y \\\\ y &=y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-2y \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ee7bcb0-cbaf-5352-92b0-cd166136549a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414160} {:answer/id #uuid "4c9f17f4-9dc8-5361-a789-bdbc15bc853f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414163} {:answer/id #uuid "584317fd-30c4-5e13-a6b5-997c0e64fc09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414165} {:answer/id #uuid "5995deb2-fa58-566a-aaf9-2112bbd190f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414167} {:answer/id #uuid "80f48683-4475-5276-86de-70b5aaa6717e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ee7bcb0-cbaf-5352-92b0-cd166136549a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414160} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7896c9b-7e0a-54c6-99f6-7e5e3f97a0cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414182}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66e690c7-cd96-576d-8320-9b08eb6ce160" :question/math-academy-id "q-73741" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -10 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Reducing an Augmented Matrix for a Singular 2x2 System to REF and Solving the Resulting System"}]}
